{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1491639-clarification-on-opacity","id":1491639,"title":"Clarification on Opacity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-28T12:59:18-07:00","id":1491639,"title":"Clarification on Opacity","content":"My read of the mechanics for Mysteries is that the player doesn't know the Opacity rating, and therefore doesn't know many successes they need to accumulate during Scrutiny to reduce it. Do I have that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T14:32:50-07:00","id":1491655,"title":"","content":"Correct, maybe with a knowing of Prime you could, but by default players do not know. However, be careful when setting the Opacity level, the difficulty increase is non-linear. A difficulty 4 Opacity requires 10 successes (4+3+2+1), a Opacity 5 needs 15 and Opacity 6 requires 21.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-28-2022, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T14:40:41-07:00","id":1491660,"title":"","content":"Thanks for confirming. I also figured from a narrative perspective outright telling them what the Opacity is before they attempt Scrutiny seriously breaks the 4th wall. Can't really call it a Mystery if you know your target beforehand. Yup, the nonlinearity stuff made sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T06:56:29-07:00","id":1491757,"title":"","content":"Similar to a target's defence (or withstand) in combat, you find that bit out when you first attack them.<br /> <br /> But for bigger mysteries see the additional rules in SoS. You can have locked Opacity (needs X thing to unlock) Mysteries as Clues in an investigation, Clues as Mysteries, and a combination of both...<br /> <br /> And linked Opacities, where fully revealing one mystery reduces the Opacity of the linked mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-29-2022, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}